{"annotations": [], "blocks": [{"bbox": [48.1889, 87.59993399999996, 535.31533562, 147.15223175999995], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 0, "source": "docling", "text": "Add-on parsaclisib for patients with myelofibrosis and suboptimal response to ruxolitinib: a randomized phase 3 study"}, {"bbox": [48.1889, 154.52448399999992, 509.7810675, 211.67275805999998], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 1, "source": "docling", "text": "Jean-Jacques Kiladjian 1 , Uma Borate 2 , Elisabetta Abruzzese 3 , Valerio De Stefano 4 , Tiejun Gong 5 , Massimo Breccia 6 , Francesca Palandri 7 , Fabrizio Pane 8 , Andrea Patriarca 9 , Hakon Reikvam 10,11 , Lindsay Rein 12 , Abdulraheem Yacoub 13 , Feng Zhou 14 , Michael Stouffs 14 , Albert Assad 14, * , , Alessandro Maria Vannucchi 15"}, {"bbox": [48.1889, 229.88554999999997, 282.39330926, 238.73597800000005], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 2, "source": "docling", "text": "1 Saint-Louis Hospital, Paris Cit � e University, INSERM, Paris 75010, France"}, {"bbox": [48.1889, 239.91954999999996, 530.0382136599999, 258.74825257], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 3, "source": "docling", "text": "2 Division of Hematology, The Ohio State University Comprehensive Cancer Center, Arthur G. James Cancer Hospital and Richard J. Solove Research Institute, The James Outpatient Care, Columbus, OH 43210, United States"}, {"bbox": [48.1889, 259.93255, 253.09687547, 268.72697800000003], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 4, "source": "docling", "text": "3 S. Eugenio Hospital, Tor Vergata University, Rome 00144, Italy"}, {"bbox": [48.1889, 269.91054999999994, 528.1038378400001, 288.73845328], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 5, "source": "docling", "text": "4 Section of Hematology, Department of Radiological and Hematological Sciences, Catholic University, Fondazione Policlinico Gemelli IRCCS, Rome 00168, Italy"}, {"bbox": [48.1889, 289.92254999999994, 402.40300912, 298.716978], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 6, "source": "docling", "text": "5 Harbin Institute of Hematology and Oncology, Harbin the First Hospital, Harbin, Heilongjiang 150010, China"}, {"bbox": [48.1889, 299.90054999999995, 451.40719656, 308.75197799999995], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 7, "source": "docling", "text": "6 Department of Translational and Precision Medicine, Azienda Policlinico Umberto I, Sapienza University, Rome 00161, Italy"}, {"bbox": [48.1889, 309.87854999999996, 442.73370498, 318.72997799999996], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 8, "source": "docling", "text": "7 Department of Medical and Surgical Sciences, IRCCS Azienda Ospedaliero-Universitaria di Bologna, Bologna 40138, Italy"}, {"bbox": [48.1889, 319.91355, 335.07425074, 328.7649779999999], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 9, "source": "docling", "text": "8 Department of Clinical Medicine and Surgery, University Federico II, Naples 80131, Italy"}, {"bbox": [48.1889, 329.89154999999994, 434.96660207, 338.74197799999996], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 10, "source": "docling", "text": "9 Division of Hematology, Department of Translational Medicine, Universit � a del Piemonte Orientale, Novara 28100, Italy"}, {"bbox": [48.1889, 339.92654999999996, 53.93670839999999, 344.61915], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 11, "source": "docling", "text": "10"}, {"bbox": [54.0283, 341.68106599999993, 447.6825792600001, 348.72097799999995], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 12, "source": "docling", "text": "Department of Clinical Science, K.G. Jebsen Center for Myeloid Blood Cancer, University of Bergen, Bergen 5009, Norway"}, {"bbox": [48.1889, 349.90455, 311.05308715, 358.75497799999994], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 13, "source": "docling", "text": "11 Department of Medicine, Haukeland University Hospital, Bergen, 5009, Norway"}, {"bbox": [48.1889, 359.88154999999995, 365.23560985999995, 368.73297799999995], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 14, "source": "docling", "text": "12 Department of Medicine, Duke University School of Medicine, Durham, NC 27710, United States"}, {"bbox": [48.1889, 369.91655, 467.33913355, 378.71097799999995], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 15, "source": "docling", "text": "13 Department of Internal Medicine, University of Kansas Medical Center, Westwood Campus, Westwood, KS 66205, United States"}, {"bbox": [48.1889, 379.89455, 239.37798310000005, 388.745978], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 16, "source": "docling", "text": "14 Incyte Corporation, Wilmington, DE 19803, United States"}, {"bbox": [48.1889, 389.92954999999995, 503.21228513, 398.72397799999993], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 17, "source": "docling", "text": "15 Department of Experimental and Clinical Medicine, University of Florence, Azienda Ospedaliero-Universitaria Careggi, Florence 50134, Italy"}, {"bbox": [48.189172989999996, 401.71834056999995, 546.82214, 418.73572784999993], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 18, "source": "docling", "text": "*Corresponding author: Albert Assad, MD, Incyte Corporation, Oncology Drug Development, 1801 Augustine Cut-Off, Wilmington, DE 19803, United States (aassad@incyte.com)."}, {"bbox": [48.1889, 442.128066, 99.49950530000001, 453.567978], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 19, "source": "docling", "text": "Abstract"}, {"bbox": [48.1889, 461.33299999999997, 554.6652499999999, 517.7117], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 20, "source": "docling", "text": "Background: Ruxolitinib  (JAK1/JAK2  inhibitor)  is  indicated  for  adults  with  intermediate  or  high-risk  myelofibrosis; however, a subset of patients may exhibit a suboptimal response due to persistent PI3K/AKT activation. The phase 3, randomized,  double-blind,  placebo-controlled  LIMBER-304  study  (NCT04551053)  investigated  the  efficacy  and  safety  of add-on parsaclisib (highly selective PI3K δ inhibitor) in patients with myelofibrosis and suboptimal or declining response to stable ruxolitinib monotherapy."}, {"bbox": [48.1889, 527.3798499999999, 554.6557500000001, 571.7898166666666], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 21, "source": "docling", "text": "Patients and Methods: Adults with primary or secondary myelofibrosis who received ruxolitinib with palpable spleen and Myelofibrosis Symptom Assessment Form (MFSAF) total symptom score (TSS) ≥ 10  were  eligible.  Primary  end  point  was proportion of patients achieving ≥ 25% spleen volume reduction (SVR; baseline to week 24); key secondary end point was proportion of patients with ≥ 50% MFSAF-TSS reduction (baseline to week 24)."}, {"bbox": [48.1889, 581.3512499999999, 554.65765, 661.7108], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 22, "source": "docling", "text": "Results: In total, 90 patients received parsaclisib/ruxolitinib; 87 received placebo/ruxolitinib. At week 24, 16.7% of patients receiving  parsaclisib/ruxolitinib  achieved ≥ 25% SVR vs 9.7% for placebo/ruxolitinib; this difference  was  not  statistically significant. By week 24, ≥ 50% reduction in MFSAF-TSS was observed in 17.1% of patients receiving parsaclisib/ruxolitinib vs  14.1%  for  placebo/ruxolitinib.  Higher  rates  of  infections  (including  cytomegalovirus)  and  gastrointestinal  disorders were observed with parsaclisib/ruxolitinib.  Grade ≥ 3  treatment-emergent adverse events occurred in  60.0% of  patients receiving  parsaclisib/ruxolitinib  vs  42.5%  with  placebo/ruxolitinib.  The  study  was  terminated  early  based  on  efficacy findings."}, {"bbox": [48.1889, 724.8319655199999, 202.29449065, 730.3320535199999], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 23, "source": "docling", "text": "© The Author(s) 2026. Published by Oxford University Press."}], "checksum": "f70c6d8a6ae74f44ad94aad2939c5e64d6c542c82a965d36532bff2cbfd0ce66", "content_present": true, "doc_id": "d-730339a6f12064a3", "docling_version": "2.118.0", "engine_version": "2.118.0", "errors": [], "images": [], "page_index": 0, "page_sizes": {"1": [595.2760009765625, 782.3619995117188]}, "route": "docling", "schema_version": "v0.1.0", "source_hash": "730339a6f12064a3ce1677bdb0cc37f7165e2a98364d9c7cb4512c3130599815", "status": "ok", "tables": [], "timings": {}}